<section id="practice" class="practice dark section-pad" aria-labelledby="practice-title"><div class="practice-intro"><p class="eyebrow mono">04 / A QUICK THOUGHT EXPERIMENT</p><h2 id="practice-title">An answer is good.<br>Knowing <span class="serif">why</span><br>is better.</h2><p>Take the idea out of the lab.<br>One original practice question. No scorekeeping.</p><span class="mono tag">CONCEPT CHECK · NOT AN OFFICIAL EXAM ITEM</span></div><form id="practice-form" data-practice><fieldset><legend>In our first-order model, you double the initial concentration while keeping temperature, surface area and catalyst unchanged. What happens?</legend><label><input type="radio" name="answer" value="k"><span class="answer-letter mono">A</span><span>The rate constant doubles.</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="answer" value="rate"><span class="answer-letter mono">B</span><span>The initial reaction rate doubles.</span></label><label><input type="radio" name="answer" value="half"><span class="answer-letter mono">C</span><span>The final product concentration halves.</span></label></fieldset><div class="practice-actions"><button disabled type="submit" class="button primary">Check my reasoning <span aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ui-icon" data-icon="arrow-up-right" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#icon-arrow-up-right"></use></svg></span></button><button disabled id="hint-button" type="button" class="text-link" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="hint">A little hint +</button></div><p id="hint" hidden>For this model, rate = k[A]. Which quantity changes when you change only [A]₀?</p><p id="practice-feedback" role="status"></p><details class="static-answer"><summary>Read the model answer</summary><p>The initial reaction rate doubles because rate = k[A]₀. The rate constant stays unchanged; in this irreversible 1:1 model the final product concentration also doubles.</p></details><noscript><p class="no-js-note">The model answer is available above. Enable JavaScript for feedback and a hint.</p></noscript></form></section>
